      "The ceiling visible after popcorn removal is usually not the ceiling homeowners expected to paint. Texture can hide builder-grade joints, uneven compound, old leak repairs, paper damage, fastener marks, and broad waves for decades. Removing it exposes the actual substrate. That does not automatically mean the removal failed; it means the finishing scope can finally be judged accurately.",
